parts.bearing.deepgroove


# name: <cell-element>
# type: sq_string
# elements: 1
# length: 2332
parts: B = parts.bearing.deepgroove ('data')
parts: B = parts.bearing.deepgroove ('data', DESIGNATION)
parts: S = parts.bearing.deepgroove ('solid', DESIGNATION)
Single row deep groove ball bearings from the catalogue.

B = parts.bearing.deepgroove ('data') returns every
bearing in the catalogue as a table, one row per bearing, sorted by bore,
then outside diameter, then width.
B = parts.bearing.deepgroove ('data',
DESIGNATION) returns the one bearing named, such as '6205'
or '61930 MA'. Nothing is built.

S = parts.bearing.deepgroove ('solid',
DESIGNATION) builds the bearing as a solid.Shape, its axis
on the z axis, one face on the xy plane and the other at
z = B: the inner and the outer ring, each with its
raceway, and the balls between them, each a solid of its own; the cage
is left out. The catalogue gives no internal geometry, so the shape
takes the proportions of the type: balls
of diameter Dw = min (0.3*(D - d), 0.8*B) on the pitch circle
(d + D)/2, as many as fill 60 per cent of it; each ring stops
0.3*Dw short of the pitch circle, with a groove of radius
0.52*Dw, so that the balls run free; the outer corners of the
rings are rounded to r. It shows the bearing; it does not stand
for the maker's internal design.

The table has these variables, each with its unit and its description,
which summary (B) lists; lengths are in millimetres, loads
in newtons:

designation the designation, as SKF prints it
d bore diameter
D outside diameter
B width
r smallest chamfer of the rings, r_{1,2} min
da smallest diameter of a shaft shoulder,
d_a min
Da largest diameter of a housing shoulder,
D_a max
ra largest fillet radius at a shoulder, r_a max
C basic dynamic load rating
C0 basic static load rating
nlim limiting speed, revolutions per minute
mass mass, in kilograms
source the catalogue page the values were read from

The catalogue

The open bearings of the series 618, 619, 60 and 62, bores 4 to 380 mm,
transcribed from the product tables of the SKF catalogue Rolling
bearings (PUB BU/P1 17000 EN), section 1.1, pages 260 to 302. Where
SKF lists a bearing only with a brass cage, such as '61930 MA',
that is the one given. The boundary dimensions follow ISO 15 and hold for
any maker; the load ratings and the speed are SKF's, and another maker's
differ.

