smallest first. P = parts.dowel ('data', D)
returns the pins of diameter D millimetres, one for each length in
stock, and P = parts.dowel ('data', D,
L) the one L long. Nothing is built.

S = parts.dowel ('solid', D, L) builds
the pin of diameter D as a solid.Shape L long, whether
or not that length is in stock: its axis on the z axis, from
z = 0 to L.

Name/Value pairs:

'Detailed'
For 'solid': true chamfers both ends c along the axis
at 15 degrees. By default (false) the pin is a plain cylinder.

The table has these variables, each with its unit and its description,
which summary (P) lists; lengths are in millimetres:

d nominal diameter, toleranced m6
l length
c chamfer at each end, approximate
maker maker
article maker's article number
source catalogue and pages the pin was read from

The catalogue

REYHER, The Catalogue, edition 2020.04, English, pages 374 and
375: article 08734.001, steel, type A, through-hardened, every diameter
ISO 8734 defines, 1 to 20 mm, with the lengths in stock. Left out: the
14 mm pin REYHER also sells, a diameter ISO 8734 does not define. The
pins REYHER sells under DIN 6325, which ISO 8734 replaced, are not
included.

The chamfer c from Table 1 of ISO 8734:1997, as adopted word for
word in IS 6689:2003, and REYHER's Technical Information (2019,
TI-116).

